### Authentication Context in Callable Functions

Source: https://context7.com/firebase/firebase-functions/llms.txt

This function shows how to access user authentication data within a callable function. It automatically verifies the Firebase Auth token and provides access to user information and custom claims via `request.auth`. It includes checks for authentication status and specific admin claims.

```typescript
import { onCall, HttpsError } from "firebase-functions/v2/https";
import * as admin from "firebase-admin";

export const adminOperation = onCall({
  enforceAppCheck: true
}, async (request) => {
  const auth = request.auth;

  if (!auth) {
    throw new HttpsError("unauthenticated", "Authentication required");
  }

  // Check custom claims
  const customClaims = auth.token;
  if (!customClaims.admin) {
    throw new HttpsError("permission-denied", "Admin access required");
  }

  // Perform admin operation
  const users = await admin.auth().listUsers(100);

  return {
    userCount: users.users.length,
    performedBy: auth.uid
  };
});

```

