### Create HTTPS Request Handler with TypeScript

Source: https://context7.com/firebase/firebase-functions/llms.txt

Defines an HTTP endpoint using `firebase-functions/v2/https` that handles incoming requests with Express-style objects. It processes query parameters, logs requests, and returns JSON responses. Dependencies include `firebase-functions` and `@google-cloud/functions-framework`.

```typescript
import { onRequest } from "firebase-functions/v2/https";
import * as logger from "firebase-functions/logger";

export const api = onRequest({ 
  region: "us-central1",
  memory: "256MiB",
  timeoutSeconds: 60,
  cors: true
}, async (request, response) => {
  try {
    const { name } = request.query;
    logger.info("Processing request", { queryParams: request.query });

    if (!name) {
      response.status(400).json({ error: "Name parameter required" });
      return;
    }

    response.json({
      message: `Hello ${name}!`,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
    });
  } catch (error) {
    logger.error("Request failed", error);
    response.status(500).json({ error: "Internal server error" });
  }
});
```

### Firebase SDK for Cloud Functions > Callable Functions

Source: https://context7.com/firebase/firebase-functions/llms.txt

Create callable functions that client applications can invoke directly using Firebase SDKs. These functions benefit from automatic authentication, meaning they can securely access user information. They also support input validation and can throw specific `HttpsError` types for detailed error handling on the client-side. Configuration options include region, enforcing App Check, and specifying allowed CORS origins.

